# Machine-local activation state (ADR-0022 decision 3). These carry owned-path hashes,
# tool identities, and trust state for THIS physical checkout, so committing them would
# publish one machine's private receipt plane into a portable tree.
#
# Two siblings in that root are deliberately NOT listed here, and neither omission is an
# oversight — do not "tidy" either one into the list, because doing so silently defeats a
# decision the activation engine depends on:
#   * `.agentic-sdlc/repo.toml` — ADR-0022 decision 2 makes it the one tracked, public file
#     in that root. The engine relies on seeing it in its Git projection to refuse a DIRTY
#     manifest; hidden, an uncommitted edit to repository policy rides along inside an
#     approved activation.
#   * `.agentic-sdlc/rightsize/` — rendered recommendation artifacts a reader may commit, so
#     they stay visible for the same reason. Hiding them would let the same file behave
#     differently tracked versus untracked.
# Both carve-outs are enforced in the projection filter in
# `skills/agentic-sdlc/tools/activation-planner.py`; search for "stays VISIBLE to the Git
# projection" rather than a line number, which drifts.
.agentic-sdlc/receipts/
.agentic-sdlc/transactions/
